## 2. Core Thesis

**Research question**: Can AI systems discover transferable structure across related dynamical systems, and does this transfer improve with experience?

**Null hypothesis**: LLM performance on sequential tasks is indistinguishable from independent (no-context) performance — Φ_sequential(n) grows linearly at the same rate as Φ_independent(n).

**Alternative hypothesis**: Agents that build internal models of dynamical structure show superlinear Φ(n) growth, with acceleration within family blocks (within-family learning) and at family boundaries (cross-family transfer).

**Why dynamical systems**: They provide anti-gaming by mathematical necessity (sensitivity to initial conditions defeats memorisation), continuous tunable difficulty (parameter tweaks smoothly change complexity), cheap exact verification (iterate and compare), and a deep mathematical theory (ergodic theory, bifurcation theory, symbolic dynamics) giving analytical tools for reasoning about benchmark results.

