## 16. Known Risks and Mitigations

| Risk | Severity | Mitigation |
|------|----------|------------|
| All models fail on depth-1 problems | Medium | Include enough depth-0 problems for meaningful Φ(n). Depth-1 failure is itself a finding. |
| Pretraining contamination on standard families | High | Non-standard params + affine conjugacy + sine/circle atoms. Monitor for suspiciously perfect performance. |
| Context window limits prevent sequential accumulation | Medium | Cap task history at 3000 tokens. Test with large-context models. Token budget is a controlled variable. |
| Observation noise destroys all signal | Low | Start at σ=0.01, calibrate empirically. Include problems at multiple noise levels. |
| Too few question types to measure transfer | Medium | 6 types across 4 tiers is sufficient. Cross-type transfer (CLASSIFY→IDENTIFY) is itself a research question. |
| API cost exceeds budget | Medium | ~60 problems × 4 agents × 3 conditions × 5 replicates = ~3600 API calls for v1. At ~$0.03/call = ~$108. Manageable. |
| Statistical power insufficient | Medium | Power analysis: with 60 problems and 5 replicates, detectable effect size for blocked vs shuffled is ~0.3 Cohen's d. Sufficient for medium effects. |
| Parse failures on LLM output | Medium | Structured output format with fallback regex parsing. Log all raw outputs. Score parse failures as 0. |

