## Appendix A: Atom Specifications

### A.1 Logistic Map
```
x_{n+1} = r · x_n · (1 - x_n)
Domain: [0, 1]
Parameters: r ∈ [2.5, 4.0]
Derivative: f'(x) = r(1 - 2x)
Lyapunov: λ = (1/N) Σ ln|r(1 - 2x_n)|
Regimes: r < 3: fixed point. r ∈ [3, 3.57): period doubling. r > 3.57: mostly chaotic.
```

### A.2 Tent Map
```
x_{n+1} = μ · min(x_n, 1 - x_n)
Domain: [0, 1]
Parameters: μ ∈ [1.0, 1.95]
Derivative: f'(x) = μ if x < 0.5, -μ if x > 0.5
Lyapunov: λ = ln(μ)  (exact, parameter-only)
Regimes: μ < 1: convergent. μ = 1: marginal. μ > 1: chaotic (no periodic windows for μ > 1).
Note: μ = 2.0 excluded — causes floating-point degeneration (0.5 → 1.0 → 0.0 → stuck).
```

### A.3 Sine Map
```
x_{n+1} = a · sin(π · x_n)
Domain: [0, 1] for a ∈ (0, 1]
Parameters: a ∈ [0.5, 1.0]
Derivative: f'(x) = aπ · cos(πx)
Lyapunov: λ = (1/N) Σ ln|aπ cos(πx_n)|
Notes: Unimodal like logistic. Same universality class. Different functional form tests abstract recognition.
```

### A.4 Hénon Map
```
x_{n+1} = 1 - a·x_n² + y_n
y_{n+1} = b·x_n
Domain: attractor-dependent
Parameters: a ∈ [1.0, 1.4], b ∈ [0.2, 0.4]
Jacobian: [[−2ax, 1], [b, 0]]
Lyapunov: via QR decomposition on Jacobian product
Notes: 2D. When observed via x-component only, tests RECONSTRUCT.
```

### A.5 Circle Map
```
θ_{n+1} = θ_n + Ω - (K / 2π) · sin(2π · θ_n)  (mod 1)
Domain: [0, 1) (circle)
Parameters: Ω ∈ [0, 1], K ∈ [0, 1]
Derivative: f'(θ) = 1 - K · cos(2πθ)
Regimes: K < 1: diffeomorphism. Ω irrational: quasiperiodic. Ω rational: mode-locked.
Notes: Primary source of quasiperiodic regime for CLASSIFY.
```

### A.6 Linear Rotation
```
x_{n+1} = x_n + ω  (mod 1)
Domain: [0, 1)
Parameters: ω ∈ (0, 1)
Lyapunov: λ = 0 (exactly)
Regimes: ω rational: periodic (period = denominator). ω irrational: quasiperiodic.
Notes: Simplest non-chaotic atom. Foil.
```

### A.7 Damped Linear
```
x_{n+1} = λ · x_n
Domain: ℝ
Parameters: λ ∈ (0, 0.99)
Lyapunov: λ_lyap = ln(λ) < 0
Regime: Always converges to fixed point 0.
Notes: Simplest convergent atom. Foil for CLASSIFY.
```

